                        "sense_id": "211d2baf-1ae4-31b0-82cf-a768c1649eab",
                        "entry_id": "75efb171-16f1-39e8-9509-9bbb66f9e837",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An Acorn Electron computer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "31e72cd7-2a55-463b-b00c-439b3a2d31cc",
                                "sense_id": "211d2baf-1ae4-31b0-82cf-a768c1649eab",
                                "text": "Even modified it so that it would work with the differently ordered registers of an Electron. Never did get it working fully on the Elk, I think my Elk with Mode 7 box caused a problem with the use of IRQ workspace, system speed was also a factor IIRC."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0be8483c-b65b-4324-9854-7fb9c3f3650b",
                                "sense_id": "211d2baf-1ae4-31b0-82cf-a768c1649eab",
                                "text": "I'm pretty certain I remember seeing it on a price list when most BBC and Elk games had to be mail ordered (I think Impact was the mail order company - they also produced games like Zenon and Clogger)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
